Project Specification: Luxury Todo List
1. Project Overview
Project name: Luxury Todo List  
Type: Front-end web application  
Purpose: Help users organize and track personal tasks through a simple, attractive interface.
2. Objectives
Make it easy to create, update, complete, and remove tasks.
Help users organize work using due dates and task filters.
Preserve tasks and theme preferences between browser visits.
Provide a polished, responsive interface with a luxury sticky-note visual style.
3. Core Requirements
Functional requirements
Users can add a task with an optional due date.
Users can edit and delete existing tasks.
Users can mark tasks as completed or active.
Users can filter tasks by All, Active, and Completed.
The interface displays remaining and completed task counts.
Due-date indicators identify tasks due today or overdue.
Tasks persist in browser `localStorage`.
Users can switch between light and dark themes, with the preference saved locally.
Design requirements
Sticky-note cards use soft pastel colors, subtle rotation, and shadows.
Hover interactions provide gentle visual feedback.
The layout adapts to desktop and mobile screen sizes.
Text and controls remain readable and usable in both themes.
4. Technology Stack
HTML5: content and structure
CSS3: layout, visual design, responsive behavior, and themes
JavaScript: task logic, DOM updates, filtering, dates, and persistence
Browser localStorage: local data persistence
5. Scope and Constraints
The application runs in a modern web browser.
No backend, account system, or cloud synchronization is included.
Tasks are stored only in the current browser's local storage and are not automatically shared across devices.
Clearing browser storage may remove saved tasks.
6. Acceptance Criteria
The project is considered successful when users can add, edit, complete, delete, and filter tasks; assign optional due dates; see task counts and due-date indicators; switch themes; and retain saved data after refreshing the page. The interface should display the sticky-note design and adapt to smaller screens.
7. Possible Future Enhancements
Search and priority labels
Drag-and-drop sorting
Export/import functionality
Optional cloud synchronization and user accounts
